  displayName: Book-bearer's diary
  description: 'Third trip this month. The patron pays in old silver for every tome
    we carry into a guardian''s glade, and he never asks for one back. Marta says
    the tomes are ledgers: he writes down what the land is worth, and the land hates
    being counted. Marta talks too much. Tomorrow the Earth tome goes north.'
